00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:06,291
Did you give him a beer?

269
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:08,376
No.

270
00:11:08,418 --> 00:11:09,710
Will you excuse us?

271
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:11,129
We need to talk for a moment.

272
00:11:11,171 --> 00:11:12,922
Yeah, sure. Go...

273
00:11:12,964 --> 00:11:14,508
Oh, me. Right.

274
00:11:17,469 --> 00:11:18,761
He's miserable.

275
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:20,679
What happened to him?

276
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:22,015
Nothing.

277
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:23,933
Just talked
about stuff.

278
00:11:23,975 --> 00:11:24,851
What stuff?

279
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:27,854
Rachel stuff.

280
00:11:27,895 --> 00:11:30,689
Oh, Joey,
you bummed him out.

281
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:33,485
This was the happiest
dog in the world.

282
00:11:33,527 --> 00:11:34,944
He spends
half a day with you

283
00:11:34,986 --> 00:11:36,112
and look at him.

284
00:11:37,614 --> 00:11:39,073
He's breathing.

285
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:40,617
Okay, I'm going

286
00:11:40,659 --> 00:11:42,243
to take him back
to Wendy's.

287
00:11:42,285 --> 00:11:43,453
No, no, no. He's fine.

288
00:11:43,495 --> 00:11:44,787
Look, look, look.

289
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:46,414
Here's your ball.
Get the ball.

290
00:11:46,456 --> 00:11:48,124
Get your ball.
Get your ball!

291
00:11:48,166 --> 00:11:50,251
Get your ball! Get...

292
00:11:50,293 --> 00:11:52,546
My God, what have
I done to you?

293
00:11:52,587 --> 00:11:55,798
Huh? I broke the dog.

294
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:58,259
I broke the dog!

295
00:12:00,011 --> 00:12:02,180
Well, I'm going
to pick up Mona.

296
00:12:02,222 --> 00:12:04,641
What have you got
going on tonight?

297
00:12:04,683 --> 00:12:07,060
Oh, I got big Valentine's plans.

298
00:12:07,101 --> 00:12:09,521
I got my Chinese food on the way

299
00:12:09,563 --> 00:12:11,898
and the rest
of your saltwater taffy.

300
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:13,692
You know, it's interesting.

301
00:12:13,732 --> 00:12:16,361
Most people think that's made
with seawater, when, in fact...

302
00:12:16,403 --> 00:12:19,113
Ross, we actually watched
the documentary together.

303
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:21,157
( knocking on door )

304
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:22,659
Oop! My Chinese food.

305
00:12:22,701 --> 00:12:24,244
I'll get my cash.

306
00:12:28,665 --> 00:12:29,957
Mona?

307
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:32,168
You're, uh...

308
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:33,503
What are...? Hi.

309
00:12:33,545 --> 00:12:34,671
Hi.

310
00:12:34,713 --> 00:12:36,089
What are you doing here?

311
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:37,716
I'm supposed
to pick you up.

312
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:38,966
Change of plans.

313
00:12:39,008 --> 00:12:40,719
I made you a special
Valentine's dinner.

314
00:12:40,759 --> 00:12:41,760
Surprise!

315
00:12:41,802 --> 00:12:43,388
( yells )

316
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:46,600
Oh. Hey, Mona.

317
00:12:46,641 --> 00:12:49,436
Hi. Hi. Hi, Rachel.

318
00:12:49,477 --> 00:12:52,105
What's she doing here?

319
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:53,814
I have no idea.

320
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:56,775
Um... I'll
be watching TV

321
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:58,445
if anybody needs me.

322
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:00,905
Seriously,
what is she doing here?

323
00:13:00,947 --> 00:13:02,365
Uh... you know, lately

324
00:13:02,407 --> 00:13:04,492
she just likes
hanging out here.

325
00:13:04,534 --> 00:13:05,577
Why?

326
00:13:05,619 --> 00:13:08,121
I think she's lonely.

327
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:10,290
Okay, but it's
Valentine's Day.

328
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:12,292
Can't we just
ask her to go?

329
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:13,960
Well, no, no.

330
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:16,463
She's way
too emotional.

331
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:19,466
And, by emotional,
I mean...

332
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:21,175
( doorbell rings )

333
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:22,510
I'm not here.

334
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:24,845
That's just my Chinese food.

335
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:27,098
Oh, my God. She has
food delivered here?

336
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:29,142
Yes. She's...
she's emotional

337
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:32,103
but... but ballsy.

338
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:34,021
You know what I'm going to do?

339
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:37,275
I'm going to get in my sweats
and eat this in bed.

340
00:13:40,361 --> 00:13:43,615
And you thought she was
going to be in our way.

341
00:13:43,657 --> 00:13:47,577
So, okay,
why don't you

342
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:48,911
open the champagne

343
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:50,246
and I will
be right back.

344
00:13:50,288 --> 00:13:51,830
I've got
a surprise for you.

345
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:54,459
You got another ex-wife
back there?

346
00:13:54,501 --> 00:13:57,962
Oh... you...
please start drinking.

347
00:14:02,509 --> 00:14:04,135
I just came
to grab the phone.

348
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:05,804
Oh, Rachel, wait. Hey.

349
00:14:05,844 --> 00:14:07,096
Um... I hope

350
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:09,182
you don't take
this the wrong way

351
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:11,559
but... but, um...
what are you doing?

352
00:14:11,601 --> 00:14:13,687
Oh, I'm sorry.
Do you need the phone?

353
00:14:13,728 --> 00:14:15,980
No. No. Listen

354
00:14:16,022 --> 00:14:17,607
Ross is too nice
to say anything

355
00:14:17,649 --> 00:14:18,857
but this
is his apartment

356
00:14:18,899 --> 00:14:20,943
and we... we got to
have some boundaries

357
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:23,196
so why don't you just
go back to your place

358
00:14:23,237 --> 00:14:24,489
and give us
some privacy.

359
00:14:24,531 --> 00:14:26,866
But, Mona,
I... I live here.

360
00:14:29,536 --> 00:14:33,581
Happy Valentine's Day!

361
00:14:37,377 --> 00:14:40,880
Or something
to remember me by.

362
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:52,266
How long has
it been this time?

363
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:53,934
90 seconds.

364
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:55,436
That's better.

365
00:14:55,478 --> 00:14:57,146
90 seconds
is a long time

366
00:14:57,188 --> 00:14:58,606
not to think about it

367
00:14:58,648 --> 00:15:01,108
except all I did
was think about it.

368
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:02,777
I know. It haunts me.

369
00:15:02,819 --> 00:15:04,738
Up till now,
the worst thing I ever saw

370
00:15:04,779 --> 00:15:06,447
was my father
doing tequila shots

371
00:15:06,489 --> 00:15:08,783
off the naked houseboy.

372
00:15:08,825 --> 00:15:10,910
After this,
I would gladly

373
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:13,079
make that
my screen saver.

374
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,122
We have
to get past this.

375
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:17,250
Why don't we just
get rid of the tape

376
00:15:17,291 --> 00:15:18,918
and pretend it
never existed.

377
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:20,253
I could do that.

378
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:21,629
All right.

379
00:15:24,674 --> 00:15:28,386
Okay, now all we got to do
is get rid of this chair.

380
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:43,610
( knocking on door )

381
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,236
Oh, thank God!

382
00:15:45,278 --> 00:15:46,529
Oh, I know!

383
00:15:46,571 --> 00:15:47,614
Come in.

384
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:48,948
Hi. I'm so sorry

385
00:15:48,989 --> 00:15:50,949
to barge in on your Valentine

386
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:53,953
but I had to get away
from all the yelling.

387
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:55,538
Mona is dumping Ross.

388
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:57,123
Oh, my God.

389
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:58,583
Poor Ross.

390
00:16:01,168 --> 00:16:02,629
Oh, great.

391
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:04,923
We have to watch him
do yoga in his underwear

392
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:06,674
but for this
he closes the drapes.

393
00:16:06,716 --> 00:16:08,635
Rach, you know

394
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:11,137
that birthing tape
that you wanted to see?

395
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:12,597
It's here.

396
00:16:12,639 --> 00:16:14,098
Oh, and we
should warn you

397
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,475
before you watch it...

398
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:16,935
Don't watch it.

399
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:19,646
Why? You saw it? Is it scary?

400
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:22,106
Well, let's just say
that it's ironic

401
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:24,317
how footage
of someone being born

402
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:26,653
can make you want
to kill yourself.

403
00:16:26,694 --> 00:16:27,987
Well... well, now, wait.

404
00:16:28,028 --> 00:16:29,322
I'm all freaked out.

405
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:31,365
Come on. You guys
will watch it with me.

406
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:33,493
No, but I will
leave a sweater

407
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:36,203
that smells like me
right next to you.

408
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:37,956
Come on, seriously, you guys.

409
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:40,708
You're not going
to make me watch this alone.

410
00:16:43,962 --> 00:16:45,254
She's right.

411
00:16:45,296 --> 00:16:46,923
Of course not.

412
00:16:46,965 --> 00:16:49,425
Honey, get the tape.

413
00:16:55,473 --> 00:16:59,978
This reminds me of a very
specific part of the tape.

414
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,480
Okay...

415
00:17:02,522 --> 00:17:05,358
here we go.

416
00:17:05,399 --> 00:17:06,693
Okay.

417
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:08,068
( clears throat )

418
00:17:09,153 --> 00:17:11,030
Ooh, my!

419
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:14,742
( woman screaming )

420
00:17:14,784 --> 00:17:18,287
Oh, why is that baby
torturing that woman?!

421
00:17:18,329 --> 00:17:22,040
Why have I seen this thing
three times?

422
00:17:22,082 --> 00:17:25,211
It's still beautiful.

423
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:26,838
Ah! It's horrible!

424
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,506
I know! I know!

425
00:17:28,548 --> 00:17:30,008
I'm so sorry for you!

426
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,592
Oh, my God!

427
00:17:31,634 --> 00:17:32,927
You guys... you guys, look!

428
00:17:32,969 --> 00:17:35,221
What? What?
Did her ass explode?

429
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:41,644
No. The baby's out.
Look. It's a girl.

430
00:17:41,686 --> 00:17:47,483
Oh, look at those
little fingers and toes.

431
00:17:47,525 --> 00:17:49,819
And look how happy
the mom is now.

432
00:17:49,861 --> 00:17:51,821
Oh, Rach...

433
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:53,322
Oh, screw you guys!

434
00:17:53,364 --> 00:17:54,866
You don't have to do it.

435
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:00,162
Hey.

436
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:01,497
Hey.

437
00:18:01,539 --> 00:18:02,999
What's up?

438
00:18:03,041 --> 00:18:05,167
Uh... Mona
just dumped me.

439
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:08,170
Oh, man,
I'm sorry. Why?

440
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:10,381
Well, with everything
that's been going on lately

441
00:18:10,423 --> 00:18:12,425
I haven't exactly
been the perfect boyfriend.

442
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:14,010
You know, I mean,
I didn't tell her

443
00:18:14,052 --> 00:18:15,678
I got Rachel pregnant.

444
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,889
Then I gave her a key
to my apartment

445
00:18:17,931 --> 00:18:19,849
and then I had
the locks changed.

446
00:18:19,891 --> 00:18:21,768
And then...

447
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:24,687
I lied to her about
Rachel moving in with me.

448
00:18:24,729 --> 00:18:27,023
In a way, I...
I actually judge her

449
00:18:27,065 --> 00:18:29,943
for not breaking up
with me sooner, you know?

450
00:18:29,984 --> 00:18:31,485
Still, that
really sucks, man.

451
00:18:31,527 --> 00:18:33,029
Especially
on Valentine's Day.

452
00:18:33,071 --> 00:18:34,614
Yeah. Wait a minute.

453
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:36,532
What are you doing here?

454
00:18:37,867 --> 00:18:41,328
Joey Tribbiani without
a date on Valentine's Day?

455
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:42,956
What's going on, man?

456
00:18:42,997 --> 00:18:44,498
Girl trouble?

457
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:47,501
Sort of. Yeah.

458
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:48,335
Really?

459
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:49,336
You don't have

460
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:50,797
to seem so happy
about it.

461
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:52,006
Oh, sorry.

462
00:18:52,048 --> 00:18:54,174
Well, look,
maybe I can help.

463
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,802
Oh, I... I don't...

464
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:57,470
Hey, hey, hey,
whatever it is

465
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:59,388
I am sure
it has happened to me.

466
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:01,181
You know

467
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:04,477
actually, once... once
I got dumped during sex.

468
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:11,776
So, anyway...
so what is it?

469
00:19:11,818 --> 00:19:13,486
Oh, forget about it.
It's no big deal.

470
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:15,113
Hey, come on, Joey.
What is it?

471
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:16,280
It's nothing.

472
00:19:16,322 --> 00:19:17,615
Hey, hey, it's me.

473
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:19,283
Why can't you tell me?

474
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:24,163
Okay. Uh... sit down.

475
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:25,706
Um...

476
00:19:28,084 --> 00:19:32,463
There's this woman
that I like... a lot...

477
00:19:32,505 --> 00:19:35,382
but, uh... it can't happen.

478
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:38,218
She's not a Tribbiani?

479
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:42,015
No!

480
00:19:42,056 --> 00:19:43,516
I knew it.

481
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:46,393
So, uh... so is she,
uh... someone from work?

482
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:49,022
Yes.

483
00:19:49,063 --> 00:19:51,607
Well, uh... does she like you?

484
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,194
Sometimes I think
maybe she could.

485
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:56,696
But it doesn't matter

486
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:58,739
because I can't do anything
about it.

487
00:19:58,781 --> 00:20:00,074
Why not?

488
00:20:00,116 --> 00:20:02,076
It's complicated.

489
00:20:02,118 --> 00:20:06,205
Um... she was with this
other guy... for a long time--

490
00:20:06,246 --> 00:20:08,041
someone from work, too--

491
00:20:08,082 --> 00:20:12,211
and, uh, I could never do that
to the guy, you know

492
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:14,296
'cause we're
really good friends.

493
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:17,424
Okay, so this... this guy
she used to go out with...

494
00:20:17,466 --> 00:20:19,760
Is, uh...
is he still in love with her?

495
00:20:19,802 --> 00:20:21,554
No. I don't think so.

496
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:22,805
Okay, um...

497
00:20:22,847 --> 00:20:24,849
Is he a good guy?

498
00:20:24,891 --> 00:20:26,934
Yeah, he's the best.

499
00:20:26,976 --> 00:20:28,435
Then talk to him.

500
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:30,479
He might be fine with it.

501
00:20:30,521 --> 00:20:31,689
Oh, I don't know.

502
00:20:31,731 --> 00:20:33,273
Joey, come on.
It's worth finding out.

503
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:34,775
I mean, if you really like her.

504
00:20:34,817 --> 00:20:38,571
I do... so much I can't
stop thinking about her.

505
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:40,614
I can't sleep, I...

506
00:20:40,656 --> 00:20:41,991
Okay, Joey, you know what?

507
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:43,576
You... you have to go for it.

508
00:20:43,617 --> 00:20:45,745
How often does
this happen to you, huh?

509
00:20:45,786 --> 00:20:49,165
I mean, you owe it
to yourself.

510
00:20:49,207 --> 00:20:51,458
Here's your warm milk.

511
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:56,839
I'm-I'm going to get...

512
00:20:56,881 --> 00:20:59,008
I'm going to put
the bourbon in it at home.

513
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:00,801
Yeah.

514
00:21:00,843 --> 00:21:02,511
Anyway, seriously

515
00:21:02,553 --> 00:21:05,848
just... just talk
to the guy, okay?

516
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:07,474
And let me know
how it goes.

517
00:21:09,894 --> 00:21:11,562
It's Rachel.

518
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,825
and you need to be prepared.

519
00:21:24,867 --> 00:21:27,120
Now, you're going to make
yourself watch the whole thing.

520
00:21:27,161 --> 00:21:28,662
Just do it.

521
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:37,130
WOMAN:
I came to the big city
to become a star.

522
00:21:37,171 --> 00:21:39,548
I'll do anything
to make that happen.

523
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:41,550
MAN:
Anything?

524
00:21:41,592 --> 00:21:45,012
RACHEL:
Huh. Maybe it starts
with how she gets pregnant.

525
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:47,974
